   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking politely",
     "texto": [
      "To ask for something in a natural way, you can use **Jeg vil gerne have…** («I'd like…») and add **tak** at the end.\n\n«Jeg vil gerne have en kop kaffe, tak» = «I'd like a cup of coffee, please».\n\nIn formal texts **venligst** («please») also appears."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«En» and «et»: gender in Danish",
     "texto": [
      "English nouns have no grammatical gender, but Danish has two genders: the **common** gender (words with **en**) and the **neuter** gender (words with **et**).\n\n- **en** kop, **en** kaffe, **en** te\n- **et** glas\n\nThere's no easy rule to know which one each word takes, so the trick is to always learn words with their article. Most words are «en»."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    }
   ]
  },
